  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { For } x \\geq \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ & x^2+2 x-3-4=0 \\\\ & x^2+2 x-7=0 \\\\ & x=\\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{4+28}}{2}=-1 \\pm 2 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}$\nOnly $2 \\sqrt{2}-1$ is acceptable root\nFor $x < \\frac{3}{2}$\n$x^2-2 x+3-4=0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x^2-2 x-1=0 \\\\\n& x=\\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{4+4}}{2}=1 \\pm \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}$\nOnly $1-\\sqrt{2}$ is acceptable\nSum of the square $=(1-\\sqrt{2})^2+(2 \\sqrt{2}-1)^2$\n$=6(2-\\sqrt{2})$",
    "image": null
  },
